# halfcenter v57d clock test v1 -- THE ALTERNATION IS REAL AND IS A POPULATION
# EFFECT. The clock test in this run is INVALID: it measured the wrong signal.
# 2026-09-18. Gated on verify PASS (hash ad96f882becbee92, 22 experiments, 7.6 min).
#
# WHAT THIS RUN ESTABLISHES, and it is the strongest result of the line:
#
# 1. IT IS A POPULATION HALF-CENTER, NOT PER-NEURON BURSTING. Within-half coherence
#    -- the two quarters inside one half, correlated -- reads +0.967 to +0.975 in
#    every mechanism arm, against +0.217 in the matched-drive control, +0.152 with
#    inhibition only and +0.051 with fatigue only. So each half moves as ONE while
#    the two halves anti-correlate. That was the pre-registered discriminator for the
#    "drive 2.2x threshold lets each neuron oscillate alone" objection, and it
#    answers it cleanly.
#
# 2. THE ANTI-PHASE DEPTH TRACKS tau_a MONOTONICALLY:
#      tau  83 ms  anti -0.753 +/- 0.001   rate 10.21 Hz
#      tau 167 ms  anti -0.555 +/- 0.000   rate  6.38 Hz
#      tau 250 ms  anti -0.395 +/- 0.000   rate  4.67 Hz
#      tau 333 ms  anti -0.297 +/- 0.000   rate  3.67 Hz
#    0/12 degenerate throughout, and every arm passes the drift check (halves match
#    the whole record to within 0.01). Shorter fatigue constant, deeper competition.
#
# 3. BOTH SINGLES FAIL, AT THE SAME DRIVE, FOR OPPOSITE REASONS. Inhibition alone
#    runs away (rate 121.98 Hz, VOID) and fatigue alone silences the voice (duty 0.00,
#    VOID); together they are stable (rate 3.7-10.2, duty 0.56-0.57). So the pair
#    MUTUALLY STABILISES, which is a real dynamical statement -- though it also means
#    the interaction is measured against two broken arms, and that limitation stands.
#
# WHY THE CLOCK TEST IS INVALID HERE. The exponent was computed from `peak_f`, which
# is the peak of the VOICE AMPLITUDE ENVELOPE -- group 8. The competition is inside
# group 2, and the alternation lives in the half-DIFFERENCE, whose peak frequency was
# assigned to a variable named `f_ignored` and discarded. So the reported +0.035 says
# nothing about whether the alternation tracks its own time constant, and the printed
# "NOT A CLOCK" does not follow. Fixed: the exponent is now computed on the
# half-difference, and the rerun is in flight.
#
# Note the envelope periods were flat at 2.5-3.5 Hz across all four tau values, which
# is consistent with the envelope being driven by the pre-existing resonance and
# genuinely independent of this mechanism -- a sensible result for the wrong question.
